<html><head><title>How</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><img id="imagen" src="4_Partner_files/partnertrail04.jpg" width="90%" onerror="this.style.display='none'" style="display: none;">                                                                                                      <h3 style="margin-top:14.05pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:14.05pt;
margin-left:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">HOW</span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-family:
&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></h3><h1 style="font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 16px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: Roboto, sans-serif;">

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 116%; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">There are various ways for external parties to
participate in transdisciplinary education. Often, the initiative comes from an
educational institution that develops a project and involves relevant external
partners. Sometimes, a complex question from a company or organization will
come to the attention of the educational institution. You might already have such
a question in mind.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-US">The collaboration depends on the network of the
initiator. Research shows that external partners are often recruited from the
knowledge circle of teachers, researchers, or students (Vinckx, van Loon &amp;
Vleuten, 2022). Sometimes, collaborations are geographically connected, as with
the Urban Living Lab Breda in the south of the Netherlands.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:
116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-bidi-font-family:
Aptos;mso-ansi-language:EN-US">Another method is an open call, such as the
Academic Consultancy Training (ACT) - WUR of Wageningen University (NL).
Companies and societal organizations can also establish sustainable
collaborations with existing transdisciplinary educational settings.</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12pt 0cm;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 116%; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">During the TRAIL, you will learn more about the
different phases of transdisciplinary education: setting up the team,
developing the project, participating in the project, and finally evaluating
it.</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight: 700; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><o:p></o:p></span></p></h1><p style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; font-size: 18px;"></p></body></html>